{"status": "PARAMS_REQUIRED", "answer_text": "The organizational responsibilities for defining, justifying, and maintaining event logging include:
1. Identifying the types of events the system is capable of logging in support of the audit function (defined in au-02_odp.01);
2. Coordinating the logging function with other organizational entities to guide selection criteria;
3. Specifying the event types to log within the system (defined in au-2_prm_2);
4. Providing a rationale justifying why the selected event types are adequate for after-the-fact incident investigations;
5. Reviewing and updating the selected event types at an organization-defined frequency (defined in au-02_odp.04).", "cited_source_ids": ["au-2_smt", "au-2_smt.a", "au-2_smt.b", "au-2_smt.c", "au-2_smt.d", "au-2_smt.e"], "odp_required_list": ["au-02_odp.01", "au-2_prm_2", "au-02_odp.04"]}

