{"status": "PARAMS_REQUIRED", "answer_text": "According to CM-3, to manage configuration-controlled changes, an organization must:
- Determine and document the types of system changes that are configuration-controlled;
- Review proposed changes and approve or disapprove them with explicit consideration for security and privacy impact analyses;
- Document configuration change decisions;
- Implement approved changes;
- Retain records of configuration-controlled changes for an organization-defined time period;
- Monitor and review activities associated with these changes; and
- Coordinate and provide oversight for configuration change control activities through an organization-defined group or role that convenes at an organization-defined frequency.", "cited_source_ids": ["cm-3_smt", "cm-3_smt.a", "cm-3_smt.b", "cm-3_smt.c", "cm-3_smt.d", "cm-3_smt.e", "cm-3_smt.f", "cm-3_smt.g"], "odp_required_list": ["cm-03_odp.01", "cm-03_odp.02", "cm-03_odp.03"]}

{"status": "PARAMS_REQUIRED", "answer_text": "A contingency plan for a system must include: 
1. Identification of essential mission and business functions and associated contingency requirements;
2. Recovery objectives, restoration priorities, and metrics;
3. Contingency roles, responsibilities, and assigned individuals with contact information;
4. Procedures to maintain essential mission and business functions during a system disruption, compromise, or failure;
5. Procedures for eventual, full system restoration without deteriorating originally planned and implemented controls;
6. Sharing of contingency information; and
7. Review and approval by an organization-defined personnel/role.

In addition, the plan must be distributed to designated personnel/roles, reviewed periodically, updated to address organizational, system, or environmental changes/problems, and updates must be communicated to specified entities.", "cited_source_ids": ["cp-2_smt", "cp-2_smt.a", "cp-2_smt.a.1", "cp-2_smt.a.3", "cp-2_smt.a.6", "cp-2_smt.b", "cp-2_smt.d", "cp-2_smt.e"], "odp_required_list": ["cp-2_prm_1", "cp-2_prm_2", "cp-02_odp.05", "cp-2_prm_4"]}

