  "answer_text": "Control PL-2 requires developing, distributing, reviewing, updating, and protecting system security and privacy plans. Specifically, the plans must satisfy various criteria (such as being consistent with enterprise architecture, defining system components, describing the operational context, identifying roles, information types, and security categorizations, and including risk determinations). It also requires distributing copies of the plans and communicating changes to organization-defined personnel/roles, reviewing the plans at an organization-defined frequency, updating the plans to address changes, and protecting them from unauthorized disclosure and modification.",
  "cited_source_ids": [
