{"status": "PARAMS_REQUIRED", "answer_text": "To publish and maintain accurate system of records notices, organizations must:
1. Draft system of records notices in accordance with OMB guidance and submit new and significantly modified notices to the OMB and appropriate congressional committees for advance review;
2. Publish system of records notices in the Federal Register;
3. Keep system of records notices accurate, up-to-date, and scoped in accordance with policy; and
4. Review all routine uses published in the system of records notice at an organization-defined frequency to ensure continued accuracy and compatibility with the purpose for which the information was collected.", "cited_source_ids": ["pt-6_smt", "pt-6_smt.a", "pt-6_smt.b", "pt-6_smt.c", "pt-6.1_smt"], "odp_required_list": ["pt-06.01_odp"]}

{"status": "OK", "answer_text": "To categorize a system and its information, an organization must:
