  "answer_text": "To protect information at rest, organizations must protect the organization-defined safeguards (sc-28_odp.01) of organization-defined information (sc-28_odp.02). According to the guidance, organizations can employ cryptographic mechanisms, file share scanning, write-once-read-many (WORM) technologies, frequent scanning to identify malicious code at rest, and secure offline storage in lieu of online storage.",
  "cited_source_ids": [
